# Pawnstar opening set, for SPRT matches and self-play data generation.
#
# Generated by tools/make_openings.sh from pawnstar.book, which tools/make_book.cpp built from
# the Lichess open database (https://database.lichess.org/) - released under the Creative
# Commons CC0 1.0 Universal public-domain dedication
# (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/), so this set carries no licence
# restriction of its own and no third party's data. CC0 waives attribution: Lichess is
# credited in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md because it is right, not because anything obliges it.
# pawnstar.book's own header records the monthly export, the filters and the SHA-256 of the
# exact bytes the book was built from.
#
# Every one of pawnstar.book's 3328 lines was replayed from the start position, and each
# position it reached between ply 4 and ply 24 was kept when the engine's static NNUE
# evaluation of it was within 125 centipawns of its evaluation of the start position
# (62 cp, White's perspective); then duplicates were removed. A match with more rounds
# than there are openings here replays some of them, which is what tools/opening_icc.py
# corrects a confidence interval for - so the count below is the number that matters.
#
# One position per line, as the first four FEN fields. Lines beginning with '#' are comments:
# tools/gen_data.cpp skips them, and tools/run_sprt.sh strips them before handing the file to
# fastchess, whose EPD reader does not.
